        "notes": "Independently checked both proof steps against the current VAE Definition, generic ELBO decomposition Statement and proof, variational admissibility Definition, directional KL Definition/nonnegativity Statement and AC definition. Sigma-finiteness comes from the VAE; 0<Z<infinity excludes zero/infinite evidence; support plus absolute log-integrability gives finite density-ratio identity, with weighted terms zero at q=0. KL direction is encoder to posterior. Only identification/nonnegativity invokes the explicitly retained AC; the algebraic identity is choice-free. No optimizer existence or equality iff is claimed. Blei et al. 2016 §2.2 eqs. (12)-(14), PDF p.5, and CMU Lecture 13 §2.3.2 PDF p.4 were checked; no source replaces the local proved supplier. No diagram or defect found."
