        "notes": "Read every current proof step, F1-F6 and exact local supplier statements, including the full published envelope theorem proof. Pushforward gives the ELBO expectation; openness supplies a compact ball with an interior open ball; common null sets and L1 gradient domination permit the supplier Frechet derivative proof via segment FTC, continuous sample gradients and DCT. Finite independent uniform mixing preserves unbiasedness and coordinate L2. Empty data excluded; N=1 and zero gradients allowed; Gaussian base alone supplies none of these analytic hypotheses. Confirmed the refuter F5 inference: C1 composite need not have differentiable factors (absolute-value inner map, square outer map). Kept reader removal in step 1.1 and corrected F5 to the licensed segment chain rule without changing the Statement or its consumers. Kingma-Welling v1 §§2.2-2.4 checked for fixed-noise setup only; precise envelopes and L2 are explicit local hypotheses. No diagram or further unmet prerequisite."
