          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Suppose $0\\le t<T$ and the state before round $t$ has been obtained with finite parameters and records for all earlier rounds. The next supplied draw has an index in the finite data set. If $\\epsilon_t\\in\\mathcal N$, [F3] defines both records to be zero, so they are finite and no undefined density or derivative is evaluated. If $\\epsilon_t\\notin\\mathcal N$, [F2] makes the two density values strictly positive and finite, so $h_t$ is a finite real number; the sample-path $C^1$ property gives a finite gradient vector $G_t$ at the current admissible parameter. This constructs finite records in both branches.",
