        "notes": "Independently read the unchanged current Statement, F1-F5, all four induction steps, algorithm Definition, gradient theorem, VAE admissibility and exact natural-number/induction supplier statements. Base state is finite in the admissible domain. For each supplied draw, common null-set branch records zero without evaluating logs/derivatives; otherwise positive finite densities and C1 full payoff give finite h and G. Positive finite alpha and finite vector arithmetic give next finite state, with domain membership explicitly required, not inferred from small steps. Induction for t<=T and fixed loop bound yield exactly T rounds and stated records for every allowed supplied sequence, including null outcomes. T=1/N=1, zero gradient, initial/final endpoints checked; empty data/T=0 excluded. Counts mathematical oracle operations only: no computability, sampler cost, global convergence or optimality claimed. Kingma-Welling Algorithm 1 provides procedure context, not a termination theorem. No new AC use or diagram; no prerequisite gap or content edit."
